  - 'Shell breakdown (triangles, volume, watertight): #1 190 tri, vol 125,483, closed;
    #2 22 tri, vol 25,093, closed'
  - 'Source has 2 separate mesh shells (2 closed, 2 found before preparation). Per-shell
    fracture: ON'
  - Fractured 2 disconnected mesh elements independently, so no cut plane crosses
    from one part into another.
  - Concrete fracture safely exported 100 of the configured maximum of 101. The remaining
    candidates would create an open boundary, an extreme needle or an invalid micro-fragment
    merge, so they were not exported.
  - 10 cut segment(s) could not be chained within the normal weld tolerance; affected
    caps preserved their real edge order and closed the final numerical seam.
  - Filled 1 residual cut hole(s) after the primary cap pass. The repair reused the
    exact cut-plane boundary.
  - 1 cut result(s) retained a non-manifold boundary after both fill passes. The
    fracture was kept instead of silently returning an unbroken object.
  - Intact collision uses 2 compound parts. In Whole Building modular workflow each
    authored panel keeps its own Hollow Shell collider instead of one convex hull
    spanning the room interior.
  - 'Large Whole Building defers inactive fragment physics: only pieces that actually
    detach receive a Rigidbody. This keeps a local first break from registering all
    100 pieces with PhysX.'
